# Copy this file to ".env" if you want to change defaults. Never commit ".env".
#
# This project runs on a FREE, vendor-neutral LLM backend and needs NO key by default.
# With a local model server (e.g. Ollama: https://ollama.com) there is zero cost and
# no account. Set the variables below only to point at a different endpoint/model.

# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1   # OpenAI-compatible endpoint (default: local Ollama)
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1                        # any open model your server has available
# LLM_API_KEY=                              # leave blank for local servers
# LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=2.0                   # keep tests/evaluation responsive if backend is offline

# --- Running against a TUC compute node instead of this laptop -------------
# 1) SSH-tunnel a TUC node's Ollama port to yourself: .\tasks.ps1 tuc <user@host>
# 2) On the node (once): ollama pull llama3.3:70b   (or qwen2.5:72b-instruct)
# 3) Point this project at the tunnel — LLM_BASE_URL stays localhost, only the
#    model + timeout change (a 70B model is slower per call than a laptop model):
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.3:70b
# LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
